# museo build iOS

Tokens and components live in `museo build/Design/`. Every one renders with its Swift name in `Lab/DesignKitView.swift` (lab id `designkit`). No raw hex, `Color(red:)`, `.system(size:)`, built-in text styles or magic numbers where a token exists. Icons are SF Symbols. Light mode only.

## Tokens

| Family | Use | File |
|---|---|---|
| `MuseColor` | `ground` page, `raised` cards, `inset` rows in a card, `composer` white, `shelf` chips, `ink` / `ink70` / `ink55` text, `hairline`, `moss` primary fill, `moss600` accent text, `mossTint` tag fill, `clay` consequence, `ochre` a marker | `MuseColor.swift` |
| `MuseType` | Lora: `display` 40, `title` 28, `titleSmall` 22, `headline` 19, `serif` 17. Satoshi: `label` 15 medium, `body` 15, `meta` 13, `caption` 11, `eyebrow` 11 (+ `eyebrowTracking`) | `MuseFont.swift` |
| `MuseSpacing` | `xxs` 4, `xs` 8, `sm` 12, `row` 14, `md` 16, `card` 18, `page` 20, `xl` 24, `section` 28, `sectionLabel` 40 | `MuseLayout.swift` |
| `MuseRadius` | `tag` 10, `control` 14, `card` 20, `tile` 20, `sheet` 28 | `MuseLayout.swift` |
| `MuseMotion` | `snappy`, `smooth`, `gentle`, `drift` (a muse arriving), `select`, `dissolve`; `.museAnimation(_:value:)` honors Reduce Motion | `MuseLayout.swift` |
| Lift | `.museElevation(.e0 / .e1 / .e2)`: green-black shadows, three levels only | `MuseLayout.swift` |
| Haptics | `MuseHaptics.play(.soft)`, `.received`, `.success`, `.done`. One per press | `MuseHaptics.swift` |
| Copy | `museClock`, `museRelative`, `museDayTitle`, `museDuration`, `museCalm`, `museQuiet`, `musePlain(max:)`, `museQuoted` | `MuseFormat.swift` |

## Surfaces and components

| Use | Call |
|---|---|
| Page | `.background { MuseBackground() }` (wash plus grain, once per screen), gutter `MuseSpacing.page` |
| Card, tile | `.museCardSurface()`, `.museTileSurface()` |
| Row or field inside a card | `.museInsetSurface()` |
| Composer | `.museComposerSurface()` |
| Chip, capsule, chrome row | `.musePill(.chip)`, `.musePill(selected:)`, `.museTopChrome()` |
| Bottom fade | `.museBottomBlur()` on the `ScrollView` |
| Page title | `MuseHeader(title: "build with museo.", subtitle: …)` |
| Section label | `MuseSectionHeader("speech")`, `MuseSectionHeader("muses", count: n)` |
| Buttons | `MuseButtonStyle(.primary / .secondary / .tinted / .destructive)`. One primary per screen. Tinted for reversible. Clay text for destructive. |
| Press | `MusePressStyle()` |
| Rows | `MuseListRow`, `MuseToggleRow`, `MuseListCard { }` for several |
| Icon button | `MuseChromeIcon(_:label:action:)`, 44pt target |
| Label, count, dot | `MuseEyebrow`, `MuseSectionHeader(_:count:)`, `MuseConfidenceTag`, `MuseLiveDot` |
| Hint, code, toast | `MuseHintCard`, `MuseCodeLine`, `.museToast($message)` |
| Identity | `MuseOrb`, `MuseRingGlyph`, `MuseRingMark`, `MuseInkText` |

Don't invent a new card, chip or field style. Lora speaks (their words, titles); Satoshi labels (buttons, times, counts); never both in one sentence. Green is the orb, the primary button and accents, never a content card. Clay is consequence, at most once per screen. Grain only on the page wash. Glass for controls, paper for content.

## SwiftUI

- `NavigationStack`, not `NavigationView`. `foregroundStyle`, not `foregroundColor`. `.scrollIndicators(.hidden)`, not `showsIndicators:`.
- `containerRelativeFrame` before `GeometryReader`. Never wrap a scroll view in `GeometryReader`.
- Toolbar placements `.topBarLeading` / `.topBarTrailing`. Sheets with `presentationDetents`. Live clocks with `Text(timerInterval:)`.
- Never `ignoresSafeArea(.bottom)` on a scroll with `museBottomBlur`. No unqualified `.defaultScrollAnchor(.bottom)` on a growing list (`ScrollAnchorRole` has `.initialOffset`, not `.initial`).
- No `withAnimation` around a transcript identity change.
- Views read `@Environment(MuseStore.self)`, `RingModel`, `MusePipeline`, `AppRouter`. Never `RingBLEManager`. Previews inject `.preview(…)` models.
- Files that touch ring types (`RingStatus`, `RingModel`, `Museo`) `import MuseoKit`, even when only a member like `.linked` appears.
- 44pt hit targets. Icon-only controls get a lowercase `accessibilityLabel`. Decorative layers `.accessibilityHidden(true)`.

## Concurrency

The target defaults to `MainActor` isolation (Swift 5 mode, approachable concurrency). New models are `@MainActor @Observable final class`. Values that cross to an actor, a detached task or the model (`Codable`, `Sendable`, `@Generable`) are `nonisolated struct` / `nonisolated enum`. No new `ObservableObject`.

Don't trust training data for iOS 26 APIs: check Context7 `/websites/developer_apple_swiftui`.

After a screen or copy change, run the `museo-review` skill.
